	(text "This project exists so the main board can have a layout: KiCad wants one board per project.\nThe schematic is the same file the hierarchical project uses -- there is one copy, not two.\nEvery symbol carries a second instance path for this project, which is what lets one sheet\nbelong to two projects without re-annotating anything.\n\nThe 19 global labels are the board-to-board signals. They end here because they leave the\nboard through J1 / J2 and continue on the front board, which is a separate project again.\nThey repeat names that are local labels inside the sheet, so ERC rule same_local_global_label\nis set to ignore in this project only -- the hierarchical project is checked with it on."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
